  "passage": "A small sign appeared outside a breakfast shop: \"Students who forgot breakfast may take one rice ball for free.\"\nSome people worried that students would take advantage of the offer. But most students were honest. They took one only when they really needed it. Some later came back and paid. Others left thank-you notes.\nThe owner said she started the idea because she once went to school hungry as a child. She remembered how hard it was to focus.\nThe free rice balls did not make her rich, but they made her shop respected in the neighborhood.\nSometimes a small business can feed more than customers. It can feed trust.",
